{"id": "clm:554b37f964e8158f601b7b36e802a03a0ecac59565b4bc9a9cd562be353b1f1c", "type": "statement", "text": "The registry record for NCT07174310 lists an estimated enrollment of 900 and a primary outcome of time to confirmed motor progression event on MDS-UPDRS Part III score, with a time frame of up to at least Week 104. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)", "source_url": "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT07174310", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Anti-alpha-synuclein immunotherapy: prasinezumab and vaccines"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "structure", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5848fb52b7b9b7a59b7ed1be13aec37e77f399dc0d2cf0c19824c699f1c7e66f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:361446f6e21b3c3868b0c725d85ef36cb35ce7fd2a4543747296833cecd82c97", "ev:5c9fea2c1cabc27e90046b47b07975112c48c2826d4d2d19f37802a6caa552f8", "ev:72692255aa6097b34b6efb53af75b6040c7e6cd1a3e08b50f8cdde2766b97a51"]}
{"id": "clm:74eee0473b34c45ff155b0b625eae7c248809bcbb66a6371dda53428d667da24", "type": "statement", "text": "VacSYn (NCT06015841) is a Phase 2 trial of the active anti-alpha-synuclein immunotherapy ACI-7104.056; AC Immune states Part 1 randomized 34 patients 3:1 to ACI-7104.056 or placebo. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)", "source_url": "https://ir.acimmune.com/news-releases/news-release-details/ac-immune-positive-interim-phase-2-data-aci-7104056-support", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Anti-alpha-synuclein immunotherapy: prasinezumab and vaccines"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "structure", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT06015841"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5848fb52b7b9b7a59b7ed1be13aec37e77f399dc0d2cf0c19824c699f1c7e66f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2959c1903cf834a79e7caa2bb51e6166a9cce53924a024743b10c24d82e6a607", "ev:2bb3b82aadb7d8f35d5eae85c81920444837b274974b6c966a2c3c5dbe9003bb", "ev:97e25c7f70ef5afb16568e18d414045b940af58c852d3a60410005e28d84261d"]}
{"id": "clm:ceb490f48dbff189a961e423f31af6a28c005bb1d6a2fbb20ac293e5413c33b0", "type": "statement", "text": "PADOVA is a Phase 2b, multicenter, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, parallel-group study in which individuals with early-stage PD on stable symptomatic monotherapy (levodopa or MAO-Bi) receive intravenous prasinezumab 1500 mg every 4 weeks. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39798255/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Anti-alpha-synuclein immunotherapy: prasinezumab and vaccines"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "measures", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.roche.com/media/releases/med-cor-2024-12-19"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5848fb52b7b9b7a59b7ed1be13aec37e77f399dc0d2cf0c19824c699f1c7e66f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:32cf3fecddf18762d8c9fd2f983357afc85f37150832b03e8a00259cc0720626", "ev:ad72baa7cd57a50a882b4f86377f0ba4b8ebc5bdd7181d6560f83b366f93ffc4"]}
{"id": "clm:229ce93b77d5fdc33740bf1050930e01e62667c9b21c153279d549c1c745df98", "type": "statement", "text": "Roche reports that in a pre-specified analysis the effect of prasinezumab in PADOVA was more pronounced in the population treated with levodopa (75% of participants), with HR=0.79 and a nominal p=0.0431. (low confidence) (verified as of 2025-06-16)", "source_url": "https://www.roche.com/media/releases/med-cor-2024-12-19", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Anti-alpha-synuclein immunotherapy: prasinezumab and vaccines"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "measures", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.roche.com/media/releases/med-cor-2025-06-16"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5848fb52b7b9b7a59b7ed1be13aec37e77f399dc0d2cf0c19824c699f1c7e66f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1785696db1bf0ff4ae4f79c1addea79612c48fffe4c905ef98479579fa7316bd", "ev:4bbd9f6bd41a214aab2c5ae9146889807ea65a3dc086b7d1e96ba406d5a7757b", "ev:81b2e658081693c6dfa90974fa14d0b6d79ceee1fad416306d7cf9266f9cdcfd"]}
{"id": "clm:e06c89a6bb2ac2aafb05163df62a433d14232e179918ea8667923a8569a16639", "type": "statement", "text": "AC Immune reports that in the interim Phase 2 VacSYn analysis ACI-7104.056 induced a 100% responder rate, and at week 76 serum antibody titers were over 500-fold higher than in the placebo group. (low confidence) (verified as of 2025-12-11)", "source_url": "https://ir.acimmune.com/news-releases/news-release-details/ac-immune-positive-interim-phase-2-data-aci-7104056-support", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Anti-alpha-synuclein immunotherapy: prasinezumab and vaccines"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "measures", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5848fb52b7b9b7a59b7ed1be13aec37e77f399dc0d2cf0c19824c699f1c7e66f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4b2e2aaf0442e7c05bc2847a124b081f11e091cfa63e8e337cce8bbf86d5b726", "ev:97e25c7f70ef5afb16568e18d414045b940af58c852d3a60410005e28d84261d"]}
{"id": "clm:9197b73ae4eb4994ebd4f0d5e3c0fba6031d8c157214c2524c9fdcee01659355", "type": "statement", "text": "The Lancet's Department of Error notice states that the appendix of the PADOVA article has been corrected as of July 2, 2026. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-07-02)", "source_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0140673626013012", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Anti-alpha-synuclein immunotherapy: prasinezumab and vaccines"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5848fb52b7b9b7a59b7ed1be13aec37e77f399dc0d2cf0c19824c699f1c7e66f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:012f59b9ed8761c401d415349f0b51279e4e22218f685b5d665e5cb1431081bb", "ev:d23a5dc639d0c27f0543fedd5e9c25a8b7597f83a2b9fbf6886ef9c38116b761"]}
{"id": "clm:fd9a29d66c48927b40b28c018bd2acb78f3840193955e098a5f25957f6fd5fe2", "type": "statement", "text": "In PADOVA, the primary endpoint of time to confirmed motor progression was not met: Roche reports HR=0.84 and p=0.0657, and the Lancet paper reports a non-significant delay in motor progression with prasinezumab versus placebo. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-05-30)", "source_url": "https://www.roche.com/media/releases/med-cor-2024-12-19", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Anti-alpha-synuclein immunotherapy: prasinezumab and vaccines"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0140673626008652"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5848fb52b7b9b7a59b7ed1be13aec37e77f399dc0d2cf0c19824c699f1c7e66f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:21b50bac45458e5fe6d2d9c92e63375047f9247d1efb95be64c728f24ec3942e", "ev:824b4032ffdeea6cb73bc330dd802572471e2eca35c65d4b8f9c664c77b1c6dd"]}
{"id": "clm:0a863f7db8fdbea46a6077ccc68d12f9830d93f2dd9effa0cdd9e2d202049b63", "type": "statement", "text": "The Lancet PADOVA paper describes prasinezumab as a humanised monoclonal antibody that binds the C-terminus of aggregated forms of α-synuclein. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0140673626008652", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Anti-alpha-synuclein immunotherapy: prasinezumab and vaccines"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.roche.com/media/releases/med-cor-2024-12-19"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5848fb52b7b9b7a59b7ed1be13aec37e77f399dc0d2cf0c19824c699f1c7e66f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:03b86682c2100f0553f2e301d0c92850e08f25053c5fcc8da3e3c87d9945cd50", "ev:a343a509a53ac4ca110d4d05340737dab85e218caa9b36ee9ec6b305386344dc"]}
{"id": "clm:cb472142a255999b63c924ba5f1cbb08eb9f2c7c83c87099e668f72d9fc93c5e", "type": "statement", "text": "The Lancet paper's interpretation states that although PADOVA did not meet the primary endpoint, prespecified exploratory evidence suggests clinical activity of prasinezumab, supporting continued investigation in the phase 3 PARAISO trial (NCT07174310). (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-05-30)", "source_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0140673626008652", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Anti-alpha-synuclein immunotherapy: prasinezumab and vaccines"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT07174310"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5848fb52b7b9b7a59b7ed1be13aec37e77f399dc0d2cf0c19824c699f1c7e66f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1aaa88b8e67ea8ce9dedea2045f60ddce8894e3c7459396dd1ea7060937f6c3a", "ev:8e240d659deea2286152857c6d541280416dd2560dc93d8fa828263075ebd08e"]}
{"id": "clm:ba2633660523beeda014db2fe5bb02441c76545fac64974573f34d6c78844aa7", "type": "statement", "text": "Roche announced its decision to proceed with Phase III development of prasinezumab, and a Michael J. Fox Foundation news page described the drug as moving into the Phase III stage of clinical trials. (high confidence) (verified as of 2025-06-17)", "source_url": "https://www.roche.com/media/releases/med-cor-2025-06-16", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Anti-alpha-synuclein immunotherapy: prasinezumab and vaccines"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.michaeljfox.org/news/drug-potential-slow-or-stop-parkinsons-moves-next-phase-clinical-testing"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5848fb52b7b9b7a59b7ed1be13aec37e77f399dc0d2cf0c19824c699f1c7e66f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6d49e33016278fe0a76aeabdfd347f9dec509544392a07e713b04c3b14095918", "ev:de9921656adb38c3f08b31071a05af5d4eafe5b789f57d0e08033f166a72ec68"]}
{"id": "clm:73bd145c1cc06443f6ae22a6b5b8d8eef53ecd8a08221f045d83df7aec333554", "type": "statement", "text": "The registry record lists NCT07174310 (PARAISO) with phase PHASE3, overall status RECRUITING, an ACTUAL start date of 2025-11-24 and an ESTIMATED primary completion date of 2029-06-30. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)", "source_url": "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT07174310", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Anti-alpha-synuclein immunotherapy: prasinezumab and vaccines"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0140673626008652"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5848fb52b7b9b7a59b7ed1be13aec37e77f399dc0d2cf0c19824c699f1c7e66f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:361446f6e21b3c3868b0c725d85ef36cb35ce7fd2a4543747296833cecd82c97", "ev:63c6248aab34266aa6cf6a29da9e976ef3a7fec87d98989b95ba70c11c86d9a0", "ev:8fde4533479896501c1e2e934f6c431fe7a8d5ffa6e7cd70a109e7c82d5feb0c", "ev:d7ba5944fa6675165353b79920524aa64b6bd1497235d933f7ea3ff5a03dd5f5"]}
{"id": "clm:025a4a234dd55a541a715a3ac19edd892c168258a302de12dba90c2711d2adac", "type": "statement", "text": "A Nature Medicine analysis compared the PASADENA open-label extension with an external comparator cohort from the PPMI observational study; the authors describe it as an exploratory analysis that requires confirmation in future studies. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-024-03270-6", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Anti-alpha-synuclein immunotherapy: prasinezumab and vaccines"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.roche.com/media/releases/med-cor-2024-12-19"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5848fb52b7b9b7a59b7ed1be13aec37e77f399dc0d2cf0c19824c699f1c7e66f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:ae120b26d370530496e5c5c16d6ff26828a7dfc2cf295e93e5d9a050b22a356a", "ev:f4d43cff55a3d3aa070ff325e2fd9167c64c3bf2562f2a7a5ce4e05aec30c50d", "ev:f6de8de1806b74a2a3449d52768570aa5698725cc03722f1acdcb62343cdb258"]}
